{"moveId":"religious-interest-obligatory","sectionId":"obligation-and-consciousness","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"constructive","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":10,"endEvent":24,"startMs":17360,"endMs":61400,"excerpt":">> It means that there are enough reasons sort of in front of us that don't require insanely complicated philosophical arguments or personal mystical experiences to think that the universe exists for a reason, that it is a fashioned or created thing rather than a accidental or entirely contingent thing, and that human life has some sort of cosmic purpose within that framework. And I take that to be sort of the jumping-off point for religious exploration, interest, and belief."},"proposition":"Accessible reasons indicate that the universe is created for a reason and human life has cosmic purpose, making religious exploration and belief obligatory.","inventoryRationale":"This is the opening formulation of the motion-side burden and defines the claimed obligation.","respondsToIds":[],"responseComponents":[],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-obligation","tier":"motion","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":60,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":45,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":71,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":72,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":71,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":70,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":63,"sectionScore":67}
{"moveId":"consciousness-exceeds-material-description","sectionId":"obligation-and-consciousness","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"constructive","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":156,"endEvent":181,"startMs":317320,"endMs":381680,"excerpt":"you know, there's a form of supernatural experience this It's easy to miss it because it's right here in front of our eyes. Like you and I are in a particular way having supernatural experiences already, right now, just in communicating with one another. We are sort of sharing thoughts, hopefully, you know, depending on the how the conversation goes, uh that are very very difficult to reduce to physical descriptions of sound waves traveling from my mouth to your ears and back and forth, very difficult to reduce to brain mapping and neurons firing. Even if you can sort of reduce them to localities and say, \"Oh, this part of the conversation activates that part of Alex's brain.\" And so on. There is this really profound as you yourself, I think, would agree, difficult to bridge philosophical chasm between the materialist description and what seems to happen to human beings in conscious experience."},"proposition":"Ordinary conscious communication cannot be reduced to sound waves or neural locations, revealing a gap between material description and conscious experience.","inventoryRationale":"This is the foundational consciousness argument supporting a reality not exhausted by matter.","respondsToIds":[],"responseComponents":[],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-cumulative-evidence","tier":"central","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":73,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":66,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":78,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":75,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":76,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":71,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":73,"sectionScore":67}
{"moveId":"panpsychism-points-religiously","sectionId":"obligation-and-consciousness","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"constructive","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":225,"endEvent":249,"startMs":465840,"endMs":521479,"excerpt":"I think if you make the panpsychist move and say that consciousness is sort of a widespread property, that already takes you in a religious direction because then it becomes very unlikely that you and I are instantiation of consciousness is the highest and most powerful and most important in the universe. Not Not impossible, right? But But it seems it seems a bit unlikely. So, even I would say it's a very swift movement from panpsychism to pantheism, right? And then you're already in the terrain not of Western Christianity, but of, you know, certain Eastern religions and so on, right? And you could get from there to Christianity through various modifications. You could be a panentheist and then the next thing you know, you're, you know, you're saying the Hail Mary or something, right? So, that's one movement you could make."},"proposition":"If consciousness is widespread, human consciousness is unlikely to be its highest form, so panpsychism quickly opens onto pantheistic or other religious possibilities.","inventoryRationale":"This supplies a distinct inference from foundational consciousness to a religious worldview.","respondsToIds":[],"responseComponents":[],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-cumulative-evidence","tier":"central","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":56,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":52,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":73,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":68,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":68,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":74,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":63,"sectionScore":67}
{"moveId":"mind-combination-underdetermines-god","sectionId":"obligation-and-consciousness","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":419,"endEvent":446,"startMs":858640,"endMs":910360,"excerpt":"brain. But, I think that when you then make the move of saying something like you know, look uh it'd be really unusual if our brains were the most complex version of that. And I think maybe, but I'm not sure. I'm not I'm not sure if that's the case. It depends on how you think minds combine because there's some reason why I have a mind and you have a mind and they seem to be separate from each other. And if God has a mind which is bigger and more complicated and sort of the pinnacle version of this, I kind of want to ask what it might be made out of in the same way. Like if you say something like if you take all of the conscious stuff of the universe and add it all up together, that is the mind of God, it kind of sounds like you're a pantheist and saying that the universe is just God's mind, which is cool. That's great. But, it doesn't really align very well with Christianity in my view."},"proposition":"Even if consciousness is foundational, separate minds raise a combination problem, and aggregating consciousness suggests pantheism rather than Christianity's distinct creator.","inventoryRationale":"This is the first substantial skeptical rebuttal to the proposed inference from consciousness to God.","respondsToIds":["panpsychism-points-religiously"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"panpsychism-points-religiously","component":"Foundational consciousness leaves the combination problem unresolved and may yield pantheism rather than a distinct divine mind."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-underdetermination","tier":"central","polarity":"challenges"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":81,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":73,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":87,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":84,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":79,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":87,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":81,"sectionScore":83}
{"moveId":"pantheism-opposes-classical-creator","sectionId":"obligation-and-consciousness","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":515,"endEvent":552,"startMs":1063320,"endMs":1141680,"excerpt":">> Mhm. Mhm. I suppose I I I get a bit nervous about lumping together pantheism or classical theism. When to me these are I I don't see, in other words, pantheism as a step in the direction towards classical theism and perhaps I I think the way that you might because I think that they're in many ways anathema to each other. I think classical theism requires this separation between the creature and the creation. God is a sort of unique sui generis thing which is the wellspring creator of this world which is somehow sort of separate from him. Um whereas I think that these theories of consciousness that are increasing in popularity like panpsychism and idealism don't so much sort of posit this great big mind to explain everything we see but explain everything we see as a great big mind or as lots of sort of trillions and trillions of tiny little minds. And I feel like if you follow that that line it might actually kind of lead you away from this idea of a sort of separable creator who sits outside of the universe. If the reason we're supposed to sort of get there in the first place is because we've noticed that the universe seems to be filled with mind. You know what I mean? It it seems to collapse this creature-creation distinction a bit."},"proposition":"Pantheism and classical theism may be opposed: mind-filled or idealist theories explain the universe as mind and can erase the creator-creation distinction.","inventoryRationale":"This sharpens the central underdetermination objection by contrasting the resulting metaphysical options.","respondsToIds":["panpsychism-points-religiously"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"panpsychism-points-religiously","component":"Panpsychism and idealism collapse the creator-creation distinction instead of supporting a separate classical-theist creator."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-underdetermination","tier":"central","polarity":"challenges"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":84,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":76,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":89,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":86,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":84,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":84,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":84,"sectionScore":83}
{"moveId":"practice-before-complete-theology","sectionId":"obligation-and-consciousness","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":603,"endEvent":623,"startMs":1246880,"endMs":1291600,"excerpt":"astray? Sure, but the first step of saying you know, there's probably a higher power and this higher power is probably interested in what human beings are doing and the way they live their lives and the ancient religious tradition closest to me probably offers some access to that higher power that I shouldn't just dismiss. I think that's a very important step and you don't want to Yeah, you don't I you don't want to just hold back and say well, until I've settled completely in my mind what God means, I can't legitimately pray to God. I think that's I I guess I think that's the that's the mistake."},"proposition":"Uncertainty between pantheism and classical theism should not suspend practice, because a nearby tradition may still mediate a real higher power concerned with human life.","inventoryRationale":"This establishes the practical bridge from generic religious evidence to action despite doctrinal uncertainty.","respondsToIds":["pantheism-opposes-classical-creator"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"pantheism-opposes-classical-creator","component":"Important theological differences need not be completely settled before prayer or participation in an inherited religious tradition is warranted."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-practical-religion","tier":"central","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":67,"rationale":"Uncertainty need not bar action, but nearby tradition does not follow from generic power.","resolution":"adjudicated-existing-option","adjudicationRationale":"Uncertainty need not bar action, but nearby tradition does not follow from generic power."},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":49,"rationale":"The higher power's concern and the nearby tradition's access are unsupported assumptions.","resolution":"adjudicated-existing-option","adjudicationRationale":"The higher power's concern and the nearby tradition's access are unsupported assumptions."},"responsiveness":{"value":75,"rationale":"It answers doctrinal underdetermination pragmatically but not its metaphysical substance.","resolution":"adjudicated-existing-option","adjudicationRationale":"It answers doctrinal underdetermination pragmatically but not its metaphysical substance."},"relevanceBurden":{"value":77,"rationale":"The move materially supports practice before certainty, a central pro burden.","resolution":"adjudicated-existing-option","adjudicationRationale":"The move materially supports practice before certainty, a central pro burden."},"precisionClarity":{"value":72,"rationale":"The recommended first step is clear, while probably lacks an evidential threshold.","resolution":"adjudicated-existing-option","adjudicationRationale":"The recommended first step is clear, while probably lacks an evidential threshold."},"calibrationCharity":{"value":78,"rationale":"It concedes possible error and argues only against complete suspension of prayer.","resolution":"adjudicated-existing-option","adjudicationRationale":"It concedes possible error and argues only against complete suspension of prayer."}},"score":68,"sectionScore":67}
{"moveId":"fine-tuning-favors-theism","sectionId":"fine-tuning-and-cosmic-order","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"constructive","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":710,"endEvent":748,"startMs":1461240,"endMs":1547200,"excerpt":">> I wouldn't say that I'm impressed with it as something certainly that would it seems much more likely >> Mhm. >> Sure. >> under theistic conditions than under non-theistic conditions. And if you again imagine yourself rewinding the clock to debates between atheists and believers in the Enlightenment era, you know, if it's Hume and Voltaire or it's the late 19th century and you know, whichever time period you pick. Take that landscape and introduce into it the current scientific understanding of the likelihood of a universe like ours existing, which is, you know, on the order not of like, oh well, for every thousand universes you get one that might have life. It's more like on the order of for every quadrillion quadrillion potential universes you get you get one like this. I guess my view is if you introduce that point to any prior era of arguments between the religious and the non-religious, it would be immediately recognized as you know, better better for the theists than the non-theists >> Yeah, I mean >> in a pretty in a pretty significant way and not what would be expected on atheistic premises. Doesn't mean that"},"proposition":"A life-permitting universe appears vastly more likely under theism than non-theism, even if fine-tuning is not a conclusive proof.","inventoryRationale":"This is the principal pro inference from physical fine-tuning to a designed cosmos.","respondsToIds":[],"responseComponents":[],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-cumulative-evidence","tier":"central","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":68,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":48,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":78,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":77,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":68,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":77,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":68,"sectionScore":70}
{"moveId":"converging-lines-support-religion","sectionId":"fine-tuning-and-cosmic-order","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"constructive","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":755,"endEvent":780,"startMs":1557080,"endMs":1615000,"excerpt":"I don't think there is one single slam dunk argument for religion. I I do think that the intellectual case for being religious lies in convergence of these different lines, right? Where you say okay, the you know, the line of evidence from fine-tuning seems to be more what you'd think you'd get in a designed cosmos. Likewise, the lines of evidence from consciousness. Likewise, the lines of evidence from religious and mystical experience. And when you've got enough converging lines, you say, well, the non-theist needs basically an explanation over here to take care of this one, an explanation over here to take care of this one. At some point you just say, okay, but this broadly speaking, this looks like a universe that a mind created and is interested in you know, things we're doing and communicating with us. That's that's sort of That's"},"proposition":"Fine-tuning, consciousness, and religious experience jointly form a cumulative case that is simpler than separate non-theistic explanations for every line of evidence.","inventoryRationale":"This is the debate's main synthesis of the pro evidential route rather than a single-argument claim.","respondsToIds":[],"responseComponents":[],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-cumulative-evidence","tier":"central","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":71,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":58,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":80,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":84,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":75,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":78,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":73,"sectionScore":70}
{"moveId":"fine-tuning-needs-distribution","sectionId":"fine-tuning-and-cosmic-order","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":901,"endEvent":935,"startMs":1820680,"endMs":1886800,"excerpt":"And so much rides on our analysis of the potential possible ranges. This isn't some like observed value that we that we sort of see in the universe. It's the result of a calculation from quantum mechanics which we know is wrong because the figure it gives us is way too strong. And so I feel as though so much rides on knowing exactly what the possible sort of different options were and also knowing what the probability distribution is. The analogy that I've sometimes given is this like if I if I were to roll a a die and it came up four, what were the odds of that? You might be tempted to say about one in six. But I didn't tell you how many sides the die had. Okay, so maybe it's >> Dungeons We're playing Dungeons and Dragons, right? >> what it's got it's got 12, right? Okay, so what are the odds of getting four? Well, one in 12. Not quite because I didn't tell you what numbers were on each side of the die. Okay, it's a normal 12-sided die and still might not be one in 12 cuz you don't know if the die is weighted. And you need to know all of those facts in order to to understand the probability."},"proposition":"Fine-tuning probabilities depend on unknown possible ranges and distributions, just as a die result cannot be evaluated without its sides, labels, and weighting.","inventoryRationale":"This gives the load-bearing technical reason for withholding the claimed probabilistic inference.","respondsToIds":["fine-tuning-favors-theism"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"fine-tuning-favors-theism","component":"A small life-permitting range establishes no probability without justified possible values and a probability distribution over them."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-underdetermination","tier":"central","polarity":"challenges"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":90,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":82,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":93,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":90,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":90,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":88,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":89,"sectionScore":85}
{"moveId":"unknown-variables-limit-confidence","sectionId":"fine-tuning-and-cosmic-order","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":991,"endEvent":1006,"startMs":1978120,"endMs":2007200,"excerpt":"Now, that doesn't undo the fine-tuning argument, but I think it at least sort of puts a dent in the confidence with which many people often present it. You could I think you could change the the strength of the strong nuclear force by like 50% 50% and everything would be fine. It's just that when you consider how big it could possibly be in principle, it's like a tiny tiny amount of a variance. But we just I just feel like we don't know enough about the about the variables, you know?"},"proposition":"The probability problem does not defeat fine-tuning outright, but unknown variables and broad life-permitting intervals substantially reduce confidence in it.","inventoryRationale":"This is Alex's important qualified conclusion rather than a mere repetition of the preceding analogy.","respondsToIds":["fine-tuning-favors-theism"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"fine-tuning-favors-theism","component":"Uncertainty about the permissible ranges and variables reduces warranted confidence even if it does not refute fine-tuning outright."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-underdetermination","tier":"central","polarity":"challenges"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":84,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":68,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":88,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":83,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":81,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":92,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":82,"sectionScore":85}
{"moveId":"scientific-reaction-supports-significance","sectionId":"fine-tuning-and-cosmic-order","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":1023,"endEvent":1056,"startMs":2037480,"endMs":2108680,"excerpt":"To me, what is notable is you approach these things as a layman and you try and look at what are the scientists actually impressed by, >> Yes, right. Sure, sure, sure. >> and generally my sense is that in fact, scientists and philosophers of science have ended up quite impressed by this argument. Now, maybe to a fault, right? But that this is why you have this sort of It's not the only reason, but it's it's why you have um among people analyzing and making arguments around this issue who are not religious believers, which is of course a great many people, sort of the turn to conceptions of the multiverse, assumptions about sort of a near infinity or infinity of worlds, and so on. Um, and in that sense, you know, that the fact of that turn, which is again quite different, I think, from a lot of perspectives that were pretty confidently held, let's say, in the late 1800s or early 20th century. The fact of that turn suggests that there is, in fact, something quite striking here. It also, though, carries"},"proposition":"Although particular calculations may change, scientists' concern with fine-tuning and recourse to multiverse explanations show that the phenomenon remains striking.","inventoryRationale":"This is Ross's principal answer to the technical uncertainty challenge.","respondsToIds":["fine-tuning-needs-distribution","unknown-variables-limit-confidence"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"fine-tuning-needs-distribution","component":"Even allowing technical uncertainty, scientists' attention and multiverse proposals indicate that the observed order is genuinely striking."},{"targetMoveId":"unknown-variables-limit-confidence","component":"Possible revisions to numerical details do not remove the evidential significance reflected in nonreligious scientific responses."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-cumulative-evidence","tier":"central","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":60,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":53,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":61,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":68,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":66,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":74,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":62,"sectionScore":70}
{"moveId":"logical-range-defeats-precise-odds","sectionId":"fine-tuning-and-cosmic-order","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":1216,"endEvent":1243,"startMs":2426920,"endMs":2481640,"excerpt":"only non-arbitrary and certain way that we can we can say we know what the sort of possible limits are to think what's logically possible. Like what would just is logically non-contradictory to to imagine the constant being. And it seems like it becomes like infinite in scope. It could be literally anything. It could have any strength. It could have 10 100 a billion a trillion. It could be anything. There's no upper bound. At which point you make the sort of total bound infinity and make it impossible to meaningfully talk about probabilities anymore. I guess one in infinity does sound more impressive. >> It does. No, >> to put the precise numbers that are often so impressive. You hear sort of one in 10 to the 120th power and stuff. And I think a lot of that is is perhaps I want to say more dubious, but you know, we don't know for sure. But at the very least I think the only non-arbitrary way to do it would be be to make it infinite. And that makes it maybe a bit more meaningless, you know? Um, I don't"},"proposition":"If a constant's non-arbitrary possible range is the full logically possible and unbounded range, familiar precise fine-tuning probabilities lose meaningful foundations.","inventoryRationale":"This is a distinct and more fundamental version of the probability-distribution challenge.","respondsToIds":["fine-tuning-favors-theism","scientific-reaction-supports-significance"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"fine-tuning-favors-theism","component":"The only non-arbitrary logical range may be unbounded, making the familiar precise fine-tuning odds meaningless."},{"targetMoveId":"scientific-reaction-supports-significance","component":"Scientific interest does not itself supply a justified upper bound or probability measure for the constants."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-underdetermination","tier":"central","polarity":"challenges"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":81,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":73,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":89,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":87,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":82,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":86,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":83,"sectionScore":85}
