{"moveId":"unbelief-built-into-cosmos","sectionId":"experience-hiddenness-and-atheism","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"constructive","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":1575,"endEvent":1604,"startMs":3169360,"endMs":3238120,"excerpt":"So, there's all kinds of ways, all kinds of people, all kinds of contexts where people have them and all kinds of contexts where people don't. And it's just I think understandable for the non-believer to say, well, this all seems ridiculously arbitrary. And and we and and the religious response has to be, well, you know, you sort of assume that that there's there's an actual plan here and these these things connect to things that God is doing and is interested in doing in different people's lives. But there's no definite answer to why one person gets the profound thing and another person doesn't. And then what comes out of that is just a sense that as much as I may push you or anyone else to take religion seriously or become religious, clearly the cosmos is set up to allow for unbelief. Right? Like whatever God's up to, it includes the possibility, the allowance, that you may never, you know, that that you may not be a religious believer, right? And that's that's sort of that seems built in."},"proposition":"Because sincere seeking does not reliably produce experience, the cosmos appears deliberately structured to allow the genuine possibility of unbelief.","inventoryRationale":"This converts the hiddenness concession into a central feature that the pro account must explain.","respondsToIds":[],"responseComponents":[],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-hiddenness-freedom","tier":"subsidiary","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":69,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":64,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was t