{"moveId":"human-violence-fixes-eternal-rank","sectionId":"heaven-theosis-and-final-synthesis","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":2923,"endEvent":2953,"startMs":5818920,"endMs":5876120,"excerpt":">> But you know, if if I say like if I say, you know, why would God allow me to go and harm a bunch of people in this world? You might say something like, well, because in the afterlife they're going to be elevated and you're not. And that sort of makes up for it. But if I said to you like, well, why is it that I'm allowed to go and like you know, kill a pregnant woman and send her unborn child into the afterlife such that not only in this world that they then get glorified in heaven, but that the mother gets to go to a higher plane of of heaven and her aborted like child >> Well, I okay. Here here here >> is lowered. And that's up to me? Like I get to determine their like eternal like hierarchical state in heaven with God? Such that if I hadn't made that free decision her and her child would experience bliss together in the same hierarchy one day, but because I've made that decision, nothing to do with God cuz of course I have libertarian free will. That child is now going to be on the lowest rung of heaven. You know, that it just seems so so implausible."},"proposition":"A murderer could determine an unborn victim's eternal level by preventing earthly development, an implausible consequence of tying heavenly fulfillment to lived trials.","inventoryRationale":"This is a major downstream objection to the proposed special value of earthly formation.","respondsToIds":["earthly-progression-has-distinct-value"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"earthly-progression-has-distinct-value","component":"If earthly development determines heavenly fulfillment, one person's violence can permanently deprive a victim of the development God intended."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-freedom-heaven","tier":"subsidiary","polarity":"cha