{"moveId":"freedom-can-remove-gods-intended-life","sectionId":"heaven-theosis-and-final-synthesis","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":3057,"endEvent":3088,"startMs":6084360,"endMs":6148360,"excerpt":">> I definitely want to be very careful not to say something like when these people are in heaven, whatever it is that the mother gets that the child doesn't, uh will be experienced as as better, will be preferred, there'll be any resentment or comparison. Totally not. I have I have no problem saying that they are they're both just living the best life, totally chill, having a great time. However, if the plan for that child had been by God that they would become an adult, and that plan was corrupted by someone who freely chose to go and kill that child. Well, clearly the the sort of ideal situation, the thing they were commanded to do was to not do that. >> Mhm. >> And the fact that we're not just minds floating around, but we have been embodied for some kind of purpose, that then there must be something better or more preferable to God about us going through that experience. And it seems troublesome that I'm given the power in this worldview to take that away from somebody eternally."},"proposition":"Even without heavenly resentment, embodiment must serve a preferred purpose, so it remains troubling that another person's free choice can remove that good eternally.","inventoryRationale":"This preserves Alex's objection after granting Ross's account of contentment and non-comparative love.","respondsToIds":["divine-love-not-oppressive-hierarchy","earthly-progression-has-distinct-value"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"divine-love-not-oppressive-hierarchy","component":"Absence of resentment does not erase the fact that another agent prevented an embodied life God preferred for the victim."},{"targetMoveId":"earthly-progression-has-distinct-value","component":"If embodiment has a divine purpose, libertarian freedom appears able to remove that intended good from someone forever."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-freedom-heaven","tier":"subsidiary","polarity":"challenges"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":89,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":77,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":94,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":89,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":89,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":94,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":88,"sectionScore":86}
{"moveId":"freedom-and-glorification-constrain-world","sectionId":"heaven-theosis-and-final-synthesis","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":3099,"endEvent":3125,"startMs":6167720,"endMs":6230000,"excerpt":"there are things that are just somewhat contradictory. And you it's very hard to construct a world in which you have the freedom that you need to have the experiences that you need to achieve this particular kind of theosis and and so on. And also in that world, you can never harm anyone else, you know, you can never affect anyone else's place in eternity through through your actions, right? Um but you do have to conceive, right, of God as a storyteller who does, in the end um you know, he's he's telling a story that works with your free will and brings about >> Mhm. >> an outcome that is not the only possible outcome, right? Like to you know, to take the There's There's many different ways that you could write a Dickens novel or Lord of the Rings or anything else and get to a happy ending. And characters could have a lot of different fates and so on. Um right? But God is delivering a version of the story."},"proposition":"A world enabling freedom and theosis may necessarily permit people to affect others' destinies, while God works with those choices toward one good possible ending.","inventoryRationale":"This is the final developed pro response to the freedom-and-eternal-harm problem.","respondsToIds":["freedom-can-remove-gods-intended-life"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"freedom-can-remove-gods-intended-life","component":"The freedom required for transformative experience may be inseparable from real power to affect others, while providence still brings the story to a good outcome."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"pro-suffering-theosis","tier":"subsidiary","polarity":"supports"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":64,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudica