{"moveId":"evil-targets-specific-religions","sectionId":"heaven-theosis-and-final-synthesis","side":"con","speaker":"Alex O'Connor","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":3175,"endEvent":3206,"startMs":6329000,"endMs":6391200,"excerpt":">> That's why I answered your question very carefully earlier when you were like, is this you you seem to be asking like is this the biggest objection you have to and I'm like it depends on what you mean. If you mean, is this my biggest objection to the view that there is some kind of creative agency behind the universe and the answer is just no because you can account for it. But it is my biggest objection to particular presentations because sometimes the way in which you can account for it is by moving away from a God who has in individual instantiations of people who go to heaven in an afterlife because Jesus died on the cross for them to something like, well, to keep God moral we seem to imply that the at least the plausibility of reincarnation, maybe the existence of one self which is sort of an illusion in so far as it's distinguished sort of distinguished amongst different kinds of people and that actually heaven doesn't really work in the way that we thought and I'm totally I I agree with you that if again if if God tells me actually the way it works is like this and like that I would just be like cool, awesome. That's that's really great."},"proposition":"Suffering is not decisive against every creative agency, but proposed solutions often preserve divine morality only by abandoning particular Christian doctrines for heterodox alternatives.","inventoryRationale":"This is Alex's final synthesis limiting his conclusion while retaining the skeptical burden against specific religion.","respondsToIds":["freedom-and-glorification-constrain-world"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"freedom-and-glorification-constrain-world","component":"Speculative alternatives can preserve a generic creator only by moving away from the particular Christian account under defense."}],"burdenContact":{"bridgeId":"con-no-obligation","tier":"motion","polarity":"challenges"},"finalDimensions":{"logicalCoherence":{"value":85,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"evidenceWarrant":{"value":70,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"responsiveness":{"value":87,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"relevanceBurden":{"value":90,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"precisionClarity":{"value":83,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"},"calibrationCharity":{"value":94,"rationale":"Rounded mean of the two isolated judgments; no field-level adjudication threshold was triggered.","resolution":"rounded-mean"}},"score":84,"sectionScore":86}
{"moveId":"ordinary-practice-bears-fruit","sectionId":"heaven-theosis-and-final-synthesis","side":"pro","speaker":"Ross Douthat","moveKind":"reply","sourceSpan":{"startEvent":3219,"endEvent":3256,"startMs":6408880,"endMs":6499840,"excerpt":"you are going to church on Sunday. You are praying. You're trying to talk to God, whoever God may be. Right? And you are trying to live up to the model of what God wants that is offered by the person of his son who lived a pretty intense life on earth, made a lot of demands of people, suffered a great deal. Right? Um there is a way in which like under lots of different theological schema. Just that everyday life should be enough, right? Like you you don't like let's say you have your your you know you're a church and you have a heretical thought. You're like, \"Actually, the Christian worldview would make much more sense if we imported this concept from Buddhism, right?\" And like okay, maybe you're a professional theologian or an academic and there's something interesting that you can do with that. Or maybe you're a really intense mystic and you're going to have this experience, right? But most likely that's a distraction. Right? And the the kind of the everydayness of the practice of religion bears its own fruits that you know, are just going to be there waiting for you, right? And don't depend on you settling the question of do we need 10% more reincarnation to make God's system work?"},"proposition":"Ordinary worship, prayer, and moral imitation bear fruits across theological schemes, so speculative efforts to perfect the system should not displace religious practice.","inventoryRationale":"This is the final synthesis reconnecting unresolved objections to the original claim of practical religious obligation.","respondsToIds":["evil-targets-specific-religions"],"responseComponents":[{"targetMoveId":"evil-targets-specific-religions","component":"Unresolved heterodox possibilities need not suspend ordinary prayer, worship, and i